    "notes": "The historic Helsinki National Museum exterior as photographed in August 2012. Includes the 58-meter granite tower, steep copper spire, museum wings and turrets, main entrance stair, and the two open named courtyards. The later addition, collection and interiors are outside scope. The native courtyard outlines and mapped entrance locate the visible components. Original roof forms and materials are refined against the dated photographs."
